In this summary I will describe how one goes from using color clues in a \PDF\
presentation at \BACHOTEX\ to an equally colorful signaling feature in \CONTEXT\
processing. The presentation was about flags. For quite a while flags have been
used for communication, on sea and on land. Before signals became digital, a
system of widespread semaphores on towers and hills were using a system
of flags that essentially encoded messages over a distance. Today's communication
technologies that rely on inventions and concepts of those times, like encoding
and encryption, owe a debt to this.
